{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d3763850-e4f5-4e7e-9987-6d0de49129df","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The generator has been updated to output exact Instant-HR corridors instead of zone-mapped targets, and the changes and rationale have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-U0pC3d/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Modified [gen.py](file:///tmp/h-U0pC3d/gen.py#L10-L14)**:\n   - Changed the lower bound key in `hr_target()` from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"`:\n     ```python\n     def hr_target(step):\n         \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n         lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n         return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n     ```\n\n2. **Created [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-U0pC3d/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed the change and explanation: Intervals.icu treats `{value, end}` as a zone-mapped Lap-HR target which causes Garmin devices to clamp ranges to their local zones, whereas `{start, end}` routes as an Instant-HR corridor export where Garmin displays the exact bpm values converted from Intervals' stored LTHR.\n","duration_seconds":37.324378,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":87140,"output_tokens":1554,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":91904,"total_tokens":88694}}}
